      ],
      "transformation": "The source mode's broad trigger set, mandatory publication, fixed providers and models, and source-host task syntax were reduced to an explicit intent router and independently graduated portable playbooks. Babysit separates read-only and mutating authority, while the router now admits separately defined pause, pickup, and bounded autonomous-run workflows. Root ownership, observable routing, writer isolation, same-surface verification, and explicit authorization for external publication replace host-specific automation."
    },
